    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d854">

                <pb facs="0949" n="857" sameAs="frus:frus1918Supp01v01/pg857"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 763.72119/2261</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Serbian Chargé</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Simitch</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1918-10-28">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">October 28, 1918</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I beg to acknowledge the receipt of your
                    note of October 14,<anchor n="1" xml:id="d854-f1"/> requesting a declaration by
                    the United States, and the other countries at war with Germany, in favor of the
                    freedom of the Serbs, Croats and Slovenes of Austria-Hungary and their union
                    with Serbia in a free and democratic state, such as was provided for in the
                    Declaration of Corfu.</p>
                <p>In reply I beg to state that the United States has expressed itself freely in
                    support of the right of the Jugo-Slavs to be entirely freed from Austrian
                    domination and that at the present time it does not feel that it can go further
                    in declaring a policy which manifestly depends upon the self-determination of
                    the peoples involved.</p>
                <p>Accept [etc.]</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Robert Lansing</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
